.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ci 1  "ci " 
.SH NAME
ci \- Work with CI pipelines
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBci\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Work with CI pipelines
.PP
`ci logs \-\-follow` streams the job log over a WebSocket and resumes from the last printed line when the connection drops; servers without WebSocket support fall back to polling. `ci approve` clears an environment gate; `ci retry` re\-runs a finished pipeline.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
ci\-runs(1)
List pipeline runs
.TP
ci\-view(1)
Show a pipeline with its stages and jobs
.TP
ci\-logs(1)
Print a job log; \-\-follow polls until the job finishes
.TP
ci\-cancel(1)
Cancel a running pipeline
.TP
ci\-retry(1)
Retry a pipeline
.TP
ci\-approve(1)
Approve an environment\-gated job
.TP
ci\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
